# Single source of truth for the Azurite (Azure Storage emulator) connection
# string used by the integration-test stack. Auto-loaded by docker-compose
# from this directory; also copied onto the test classpath so AzuriteFixture
# can read it from Java.
#
# The host is `azurite` (the docker-compose service name) — this is the form
# the app container needs. The host-side Java tests adapt by replacing
# `azurite` with `localhost` in AzuriteFixture (only occurrence is the
# BlobEndpoint host).
#
# The AccountKey below is the well-known, publicly documented Microsoft
# Azurite emulator key; it cannot authenticate against real Azure Storage.
# The trailing `# gitleaks:allow` tells the HMCTS secret scanner this is an
# intentional public fixture, not a leak.
CSCHED_ROTASLSTORAGECONNECTIONSTRING=DefaultEndpointsProtocol=http;AccountName=devstoreaccount1;AccountKey=Eby8vdM02xNOcqFlqUwJPLlmEtlCDXJ1OUzFT50uSRZ6IFsuFq2UVErCz4I6tq/K1SZFPTOtr/KBHBeksoGMGw==;BlobEndpoint=http://azurite:10011/devstoreaccount1; # gitleaks:allow
